window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-24294757e701b587"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"propose-security-hardening\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">提出安全加固方案</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>$codex-security:propose-security-hardening</code>，将一组安全证据转化为结构或架构层面的加固选项。该工作流可以分析已完成的 Codex Security 扫描，也可以从提供的发现项、漏洞披露报告、事件复盘、评估文档和源代码开始。</p> <p>结果会比较不同设计选项及其工程权衡。只有在你选定某个方案并要求实施后，Codex 才会修改代码库。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-evidence\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">准备证据</h2> <p>向工作流提供：</p> <ul> <li>扫描目录，或一组发现项和报告。</li> <li>目标源代码树；如有，请提供修订版本或快照。</li> <li>能支持这些发现项的 PoC、跟踪记录、事件证据或评估材料。</li> <li>性能、内存、兼容性、可靠性、运维、交付时间或变更范围方面的限制。</li> </ul> <p>例如，反复出现的授权错误可能表明，与其在每个处理程序中分别添加检查，不如采用一个更易于统一执行的共享控制机制。证据也可能支持保留局部修复，而不是调整整体架构。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">运行工作流</h2> <p>发送类似下面的提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:propose-security-hardening to analyze [scan directory or finding paths] against [source tree and revision]. Develop evidence-backed structural hardening options with engineering tradeoffs, before-and-after diagrams, a migration plan, and an implementation handoff. Do not modify the repository.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:propose-security-hardening，将 [scan directory or finding paths] 与 [source tree and revision] 对照分析。提出有证据支持的结构性加固方案，包含工程取舍、前后对比图、迁移计划和实施交接说明。不要修改代码仓库。</div></div> <p><a id=\"choose-an-option\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">选择方案</h2> <p>选择方案前，请检查提案是否：</p> <ul> <li>将每项拟议更改与发现项、源代码及威胁模型证据联系起来。</li> <li>说明当前设计，以及新设计必须保留的安全不变量。</li> <li>比较不同方案，包括剩余风险、性能、可靠性、运维、兼容性和迁移成本。</li> <li>用证据支撑建议，并说明假设和待解决的问题。</li> <li>包含推出、验证、回滚和实施方面的指导。</li> <li>区分观察到的事实、推断和拟议设计的属性。</li> </ul> <p>在选择方案前，请审阅证据和权衡。架构图或设计建议不能替代对原始发现项或已实施修复的验证。</p> <p><a id=\"use-hardening-guidance-from-a-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">使用扫描生成的加固指导</h2> <p>对于包含可报告发现项的标准扫描、深度扫描或变更扫描，你可以要求生成加固方案集。Codex 会将方案集写入 <code>hardening/hardening.md</code>，将结构化分析写入 <code>hardening/hardening.json</code>，并将支持性方案或图表放在 <code>hardening/</code> 下。扫描生成的 <code>report.md</code> 会链接到该方案集。</p> <p>请将完整扫描目录放在一起，以便这些链接继续有效。若要审阅为方案集提供依据的单项报告，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6afd18fb00f3b1ba\">编写漏洞报告</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"propose-security-hardening\">Propose security hardening</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>$codex-security:propose-security-hardening</code> to turn a collection of security evidence into structural or architectural hardening options. The workflow can analyze a completed Codex Security scan or start from supplied findings, disclosure reports, incident reviews, assessment documents, and source code.</p> <p>The result compares design options and their engineering tradeoffs. Codex changes the repository only after you select an option and ask it to implement it.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-evidence\">Prepare the evidence</h2> <p>Provide the workflow with:</p> <ul> <li>A scan directory or a collection of findings and reports.</li> <li>The target source tree and revision or snapshot when available.</li> <li>PoCs, traces, incident evidence, or assessment material that supports the findings.</li> <li>Constraints for performance, memory, compatibility, reliability, operations, delivery time, or change scope.</li> </ul> <p>For example, repeated authorization bugs may suggest that a shared control would be easier to enforce than checks in each handler. The evidence may also support keeping a local fix instead of changing the architecture.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-workflow\">Run the workflow</h2> <p>Send a prompt like:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:propose-security-hardening to analyze [scan directory or finding paths] against [source tree and revision]. Develop evidence-backed structural hardening options with engineering tradeoffs, before-and-after diagrams, a migration plan, and an implementation handoff. Do not modify the repository.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"choose-an-option\">Choose an option</h2> <p>Before choosing an option, check that the proposal:</p> <ul> <li>Connects each proposed change to findings, source, and threat-model evidence.</li> <li>Describes the current design and the security invariants the new design should preserve.</li> <li>Compares distinct options, including residual risk, performance, reliability, operations, compatibility, and migration cost.</li> <li>Supports its recommendation with evidence and states assumptions and open questions.</li> <li>Includes rollout, validation, rollback, and implementation guidance.</li> <li>Separates observed facts, inferences, and proposed design properties.</li> </ul> <p>Review the evidence and tradeoffs before choosing an option. An architecture diagram or design recommendation doesn't replace validation of the original findings or the implemented fix.</p> <h2 id=\"use-hardening-guidance-from-a-scan\">Use hardening guidance from a scan</h2> <p>You can request a hardening portfolio for a standard, deep, or change scan with reportable findings. Codex writes the portfolio to <code>hardening/hardening.md</code>, structured analysis to <code>hardening/hardening.json</code>, and supporting proposals or diagrams under <code>hardening/</code>. The scan links the portfolio from <code>report.md</code>.</p> <p>Keep the full scan directory together so those links remain usable. To review the individual reports that inform the portfolio, see <a href=\"#/article/a-6afd18fb00f3b1ba\">Write vulnerability reports</a>.</p>"};
